1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:06,713
A ghost has lived in the peepal tree for two hundred years. A failure at scaring… and alone.

2
00:00:06,733 --> 00:00:09,093
Oooh… somebody be scared… somebody come…

3
00:00:10,263 --> 00:00:12,327
Crying again? What happened today?

4
00:00:12,347 --> 00:00:17,649
Dadi, two owls came to the peepal today. A couple. And me… all alone.

5
00:00:17,669 --> 00:00:21,595
You're two hundred. The marrying age passed long ago.

6
00:00:21,615 --> 00:00:24,870
Ghosts don't have a marrying age!

7
00:00:24,890 --> 00:00:27,591
Hmm… then we'll have to find you a match.

8
00:00:27,941 --> 00:00:33,424
But Dadi, who will marry me? I can't even scare anyone.

9
00:00:33,444 --> 00:00:36,828
Marriage isn't about scaring. It's about sticking together.

10
00:00:36,848 --> 00:00:39,694
And I have just the match. Chandni, from the well.

11
00:00:39,714 --> 00:00:42,648
The chudail from the well?! She's terrifying!

12
00:00:42,668 --> 00:00:44,695
Yes. Perfect for you.

13
00:00:44,715 --> 00:00:45,850
…Really?

14
00:00:45,870 --> 00:00:49,533
Go, get ready. You've no hair, so at least fix your choti.

15
00:00:53,503 --> 00:01:01,971
In the village's old well lives Chandni Chudail. They say whoever peeks into it… never comes back.

16
00:01:02,541 --> 00:01:05,776
Chandni! Oh, Chandni! Come out, the groom's family is here!

17
00:01:08,046 --> 00:01:11,734
Who dares call Chandni at midnight?

18
00:01:11,754 --> 00:01:14,139
D-d-Dadi… I want to go home.

19
00:01:14,159 --> 00:01:17,329
Your home is this tree, it's right here. Sit quietly.

20
00:01:17,349 --> 00:01:20,471
Oh… Dadi, it's you? Namaste, namaste.

21
00:01:22,041 --> 00:01:26,777
Sit, dear. So… this is our Chaman. Two hundred years old, and he has his own tree.

22
00:01:26,797 --> 00:01:29,181
Is the tree rented or owned?

23
00:01:29,201 --> 00:01:32,741
He's never paid a rupee of rent. So consider it his own.

24
00:01:32,761 --> 00:01:35,051
Hmm. And what does he do for a living?

25
00:01:35,071 --> 00:01:37,159
I… scare people.

26
00:01:37,179 --> 00:01:39,799
Really? How many have you scared so far?

27
00:01:41,169 --> 00:01:42,276
…Zero.

28
00:01:42,296 --> 00:01:44,724
Zero?! Zero in two hundred years?

29
00:01:44,744 --> 00:01:47,195
But he washes dishes really well.

30
00:01:47,215 --> 00:01:52,038
…Now that's impressive. There are three hundred years of dishes in my well.

31
00:01:53,008 --> 00:01:56,263
Now your turn, Chandni. Can you cook?

32
00:01:56,283 --> 00:01:58,013
I can scare.

33
00:01:58,033 --> 00:02:00,567
Well, nobody in this house can do that.

34
00:02:00,587 --> 00:02:01,705
Dadi!

35
00:02:02,055 --> 00:02:07,706
Chandni ji, let me show you how scary I am! Dadi, get ready!

36
00:02:09,076 --> 00:02:11,890
Ha ha ha! I am Chaman Bhoot! Be afraid!

37
00:02:11,910 --> 00:02:14,288
My tea's getting cold. Scare me quickly.

38
00:02:14,308 --> 00:02:16,044
Ha ha ha ha!

39
00:02:16,064 --> 00:02:17,714
You're… laughing?

40
00:02:17,734 --> 00:02:21,329
Wait. Let me show you what real scaring looks like.

41
00:02:22,899 --> 00:02:25,745
Dadi… I'll take you… into the well…

42
00:02:26,515 --> 00:02:31,237
Into the well? Clean it first. Three hundred years of dishes are lying in there.

43
00:02:32,207 --> 00:02:35,307
Dadi… are you really not afraid of anything?

44
00:02:35,327 --> 00:02:37,576
Of course I am. Of the electricity bill.

45
00:02:37,596 --> 00:02:39,082
Ha ha ha!

46
00:02:39,102 --> 00:02:40,712
Ha ha ha!

47
00:02:41,262 --> 00:02:44,430
Chaman ji… you're not scary at all.

48
00:02:44,450 --> 00:02:45,658
I know.

49
00:02:45,678 --> 00:02:50,920
But you're honest. In two hundred years, no one has been this honest with me.

50
00:02:50,940 --> 00:02:52,633
So… is it a match?

51
00:02:52,653 --> 00:02:54,773
It's a match. But on one condition.

52
00:02:54,793 --> 00:02:59,674
After the wedding we live in the tree, not the well. It's far too damp down there.

53
00:02:59,694 --> 00:03:01,605
And I have a condition too.

54
00:03:01,625 --> 00:03:02,891
What is it, Dadi?

55
00:03:02,911 --> 00:03:05,553
From now on, you'll both wash the dishes together.

56
00:03:05,573 --> 00:03:08,990
Dadi… shall I be honest? You're the real chudail here.

57
00:03:09,010 --> 00:03:11,066
Thank you for the compliment, bahu.

58
00:03:14,216 --> 00:03:19,442
And so, after two hundred years… the peepal ghost finally found a family.

59
00:03:19,462 --> 00:03:23,784
But one question still remains… who's going to be scared at the wedding?

